WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.728
Teams Phone is where a silent configuration
error has physical consequences:

2
00:00:04.728 --> 00:00:08.687
a wrong emergency address sends
responders to the wrong building.

3
00:00:08.687 --> 00:00:12.309
And the federal rules bind
whoever operates the phone system,

4
00:00:12.309 --> 00:00:13.800
which includes an agency.

5
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:19.356
Kari's Law requires direct 911 dialing and
a notice to someone such as a front desk,

6
00:00:19.356 --> 00:00:24.000
and the FCC's rules require a
dispatchable location with every call.

7
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.778
Teams provides the mechanisms,

8
00:00:25.778 --> 00:00:28.925
but someone has to configure
them and keep them current.

9
00:00:28.925 --> 00:00:32.906
So a validated address becomes
a gate on every number,

10
00:00:32.906 --> 00:00:38.425
network changes raise their own mapping
item, and a 933 test call closes it.

11
00:00:38.425 --> 00:00:42.513
Counsel decides compliance;
the catalog keeps the evidence.

12
00:00:42.513 --> 00:00:43.870
Next, SaaS.
